@startuml activity-audio-test
!include plantuml-style.puml
title Phone-driven audio test through the Pi UI (implemented upload path)

|User|
start
:Start Voice Memos recording;
:Open the Pi UI on the iPhone;
:Select the separate audio 10-line + box test;

|Pi operator UI|
:POST /api/plan;

|Pi Rust service|
:Require Real mode and idle device;
:Create attempt ID and recording ID;
:Return expected goal and pattern;

|Pi operator UI|
:Show pattern and sacrificial-stock warning;

|User|
:Confirm Voice Memos is recording;
:Tap Start test;

|Pi operator UI|
:Play 3-tone preamble + 6-digit recording ID;
:POST /api/run;

|Pi Rust service|
:Validate planned attempt;
:Append sync marker to run log;

|Laser driver + K6|
:Run full-power box + nine lines;
:Wait for run outcome;

|Pi Rust service|
:Append outcome and receive trace;
:Expose completed attempt to UI;

|Pi operator UI|
:Show upload control only after run ends;

|User|
:Choose exported Voice Memo (.m4a);
:Upload recording;

|Pi operator UI|
:POST audio to same-origin Pi endpoint;

|Pi Rust service|
:Require matching completed audio-test attempt;
:Select only its sync marker + run outcome;
:Pass audio and filtered events to analyzer;

|External audio container (analysis only; no laser control)|
:Validate shared bearer token and attempt/event match;
:Decode recording ID and analyze audio;
:Generate playable, annotated HTML;
:Return report;

|Pi Rust service|
:Pass report back to the Pi UI;

|Pi operator UI|
:Display report with waveform, playhead and run markers;
:Keep report available for physical verdict;

|User|
:Listen, inspect and record OK or deviation;

stop

@enduml